    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **35 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**, including the new `Cp25Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the rule that rejects creating an owner whose lower-cased email is already used by any other owner, responding with **409 Conflict**, following the existing conventions used by the duplicate-telephone and duplicate-household rules.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`DuplicateEmailException.java`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` mirroring `DuplicateTelephoneException`, thrown when a candidate email collides with an existing owner.\n\n2. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` that maps `DuplicateEmailException` to a `409 Conflict` `ProblemDetail` whose `errors` array names the `email` field.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 added a `rejectDuplicateEmail(String)` helper and wired it into `addOwner`. The candidate email is normalized to lower case (via the existing `normalizeEmail`) and compared case-insensitively against each existing owner's email; a `null` candidate is skipped (email is optional) and existing owners without an email are skipped. The check runs before the owner is saved, so a duplicate returns 409 without persisting.",
